     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "Not every notification is friendly, and some of them arrive at the worst possible moment of the day. When the battery hits ten percent the phone starts shouting at you, and every warning feels louder than the last. You plug in at last, and the screen settles down while the long evening finally begins to feel calm. Meanwhile the phone quietly backs up your photos in the background, one big file after another, all night long. By morning everything is safe, and your phone is ready to start the whole busy cycle again for you. Look at how people search: type a few words, press enter, and a seller replies within seconds."
    }
